 Autism spectrum disorder&nbsp;<\/p><p>Axis V: Psychosocial : Expressive screen time present.<\/p>","contact_no":"9095057890","referal_doctor":"Dr Vijayakumar","home_program":"<div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12\"><p class=\"p1\">Encourage <strong>\"Child led play\"<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"p1\">Engage at the&nbsp;<strong>\"Child's Eye Level\"<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"p1\"><strong>Give more oppurtunity<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"p1\"><strong>Sitting tolerance :<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"p1\">Sit and Play along with your child.<\/p><p class=\"p1\">Have a set of favourite toys. Gain his interest in toys.<\/p><p class=\"p1\">Engage him with his favourite toys<\/p><\/div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;\" data-mce-style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;\"><strong>Eye Contact and Joint attention<\/strong><\/p><ul type=\"disc\"><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\" data-mce-style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">To focus on EYE CONTACT for each small household activity \/ when playing with the child.<\/li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\" data-mce-style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Encourage more social games like peek - a - boo, tickle games at his level. Wait for him to respond by looking at your eyes and then play again.&nbsp;<\/li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\" data-mce-style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">CALL, LOOK, COME, GO, TAKE, GIVE, SHOW, BRING and POINT. These are the activities to enhance joint attention, i.e., the child and mother focusing their attention on an object and then doing things together.<\/li><li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\" data-mce-style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">In all daily activities like eating, bathing etc. \"Look at the soap, see foam !!! Wow...\" Show it - make him look, then ask him - make him point<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Cognitive Verbal\/Preverbal (CVP)&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Object permanence activities - hide a favourite toy or object of the child under a cup and encourage the child to find it.<\/li><li>Encourage copying lines and shapes (vertical lines, circle, square, triangle and diamond).<\/li><li>Encourage of 2 - piece puzzles<\/li><li>Teach him to identify and match 2 shapes - circle and square - Play using form boards.<\/li><li>Teach him to identify and sort colours (Primary colours - Red and yellow)<\/li><\/ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 12pt;\" data-mce-style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Receptive Language&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Response to name call - consistently<\/li><li>Encourage identifying big and little sizes.<\/li><li>Encourage the identification action words<\/li><li>Encourage following commands.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong style=\"font-size: 12pt;\" data-mce-style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Expressive Language<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Improve vocabulary using flashcards (fruits, vegetables, animals, vechicles)<\/li><li>Encourage naming action words<\/li><li>Encourage 2 word combination<\/li><li>Encourage naming colours<\/li><li>Encourage role-playing with puppets<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Fine Motor&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p><ul><li class=\"p1\">Encourage building blocks\/staking<\/li><li class=\"p1\">Encourage scribbling and imitating strokes \u2013 focus on grasp<br><\/li><li>Encourage stringing beads \u2013 consistently<br><\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Gross Motor&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Catching, throwing and kicking the ball - goal directed&nbsp;<\/li><li>Encourage hopping.<\/li><li>Encourage playing a simple game with rules.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Visual motor Imitation<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Encourage imitation of gross motor activites&nbsp;<\/li><li>Encourage imitation in day-to-day activities.&nbsp;<br><\/li><\/ul><p>Plan<\/p><p>Requires intensive Occupational therapy and speech therapy.<\/p>"}  
