[2025-12-15 12:42:08] local.EMERGENCY: Request to store neuro visit table ==========={"hnne_interpretation":"0","hine_interpretation":"0","m_chat_r_interpretation":"0","m_chat_followup_interpretation":"0","dasii_interpretation":"","mental_cluster_interpretation":"","motor_cluster_interpretation":"","ddst_interpretation_status":"","ddst_gross_motor_interpretation_status":"","ddst_language_interpretation_status":"","ddst_fine_motor_interpretation_status":"","ddst_personal_interpretation_status":"","ddst_interpretation":"","hnne_interpretation_others":"","hine_interpretation_others":"","m_chat_r_interpretation_others":"","m_chat_followup_interpretation_others":"","ddst_interpretation_others":"","cbcl_interpretation":"","cbcl_interpretation_status":null,"clusters":null,"motor_development_quotient":"","mental_development_quotient":"","tone_type":0,"others":0,"others_asymmetric":null,"baby_behavior":"<p>Combinational play (presentational play) was present.<br>On observation, she was found to be active and restless. Her sitting tolerance was poor. Inattention was significantly noted. Eye contact was predominantly absent, momentarily present. Lateral gazing was observed. Responses to name-calling were absent during the session. Joint attention was absent. Object engagement was observed during the session. Instrumental pointing was present, but single-finger pointing was absent during the session. She had difficulty comprehending simple commands during the administration of the activities. Stereotypical vocalisation was observed. Combinational play (presentational play) was present. Fascination with turning pages of a book, lining up toys and wheeled toys. Repetitive behaviour, tiptoe walking, hand gazing, to and fro walking and jumping were observed during the session. Episodes of temper tantrums, like screaming and occasionally hitting his mother were observed, with the antecedent being not given her interested toys. Mouthing of toys were observed.<br>Cognition<br>She could place all the pegs and shapes on the pegboard and formboard. The stirring of a spoon in the cup was seen. Combinational play (presentational play) was present. She could attend to the object permanence activities but had difficulty in higher-level activities. Because of her inattention she didn't match colours and pictures.&nbsp;<br>Receptive Communication<br>She attended the play routine during the session, but it was less than 30 seconds. Responds to requests for social routines that were briefly -present. As she had difficulty comprehending simple commands, she did not attend to identifying pictures, body parts, clothing, action series, or understanding object use.<br>Expressive Communication<br>Babbling was present. Instrumental pointing was present, but single-finger pointing was absent during the session. One-word approximations were absent. She had difficulty in directing the attention of the adult to objects to make her wants known. Meaningful words were absent. Stereotypical vocalization was observed.<br>Fine motor<br>She could stack up to 8-10 cubes. A neat pincer grasp was present. Scribbling was seen. A transitional tripod pencil grasp was noted. She was able to put the coins inside the bottle. She could disconnect the building blocks and connect them. Imitation of strokes was absent. She had difficulty in imitating the train model and replicating the bridge model.&nbsp;<br>Gross motor<br>She was able to walk without support. Unsupported squatting was present. She could climb stairs up and down with the alternative foot on each step with support. Coordinated running was seen. Balance on each foot for 2 seconds without support. She could throw the ball, but not goal-directed. &nbsp;She had difficulty walking on the footpath.<br>As she had difficulty comprehending simple instructions, further items couldn't be administered.<br><\/p>","baby_background":"<p>Pregnancy: Planned<\/p><p>AN period - Supervised, Uneventful&nbsp;<\/p><p>Peri \/postnatal period: Full term \/ LSCS<\/p><p>Birth Asphyxia - Absent&nbsp;<\/p><p>NICU Stay: Absent; No of Days : 0<\/p><p><strong>Developmental Milestones :<\/strong><\/p><p>Delay: Present<\/p><p>Motor - Walking @ 1 year 6 months<\/p><p>Language: First word - 1 year 3 months<\/p><p>Predominantly language delay<\/p>","visit_date":"2025-12-06","visit_time":"10","visit_min":"59","visit_session":"AM","mental_development_age":"","motor_development_age":"","chronological_year":"3","chronological_month":"4","chronological_days":"8","corrected_year":"3","corrected_month":"3","corrected_days":"21","recommendation":"<p><br><\/p>","confidential_background_details":"<p><br><\/p>","appointment_type":"New Appointment","review":null,"review_time":"9","review_min":"30","review_session":"AM","head_circumference":"","current_weight_g":"","current_ofc":"","current_length":"","fee_status":"on","fee_amount":"4700","no_fee_reason":null,"referral_status":0,"referral_to":null,"mental_prior_pass":0,"mental_rest_fail":0,"motor_prior_pass":0,"motor_rest_fail":0,"motor_cluster_1":0,"motor_cluster_2":0,"motor_cluster_3":0,"motor_cluster_4":0,"motor_cluster_5":0,"motor_cluster_pr_1":null,"motor_cluster_pr_2":null,"motor_cluster_pr_3":null,"motor_cluster_pr_4":null,"motor_cluster_pr_5":null,"motor_cluster_remarks_1":null,"motor_cluster_remarks_2":null,"motor_cluster_remarks_3":null,"motor_cluster_remarks_4":null,"motor_cluster_remarks_5":null,"mental_cluster_1":0,"mental_cluster_2":0,"mental_cluster_3":0,"mental_cluster_4":0,"mental_cluster_5":0,"mental_cluster_6":0,"mental_cluster_7":0,"mental_cluster_8":0,"mental_cluster_9":0,"mental_cluster_10":0,"mental_cluster_pr_1":null,"mental_cluster_pr_2":null,"mental_cluster_pr_3":null,"mental_cluster_pr_4":null,"mental_cluster_pr_5":null,"mental_cluster_pr_6":null,"mental_cluster_pr_7":null,"mental_cluster_pr_8":null,"mental_cluster_pr_9":null,"mental_cluster_pr_10":null,"mental_cluster_remarks_1":null,"mental_cluster_remarks_2":null,"mental_cluster_remarks_3":null,"menta